    "analysis": "To construct a laddered bond portfolio for a 5-year horizon, we propose a structure with increasing maturity buckets each year. For investment-grade securities only, we recommend the following laddered maturity structure for a 5-year horizon, with each bucket representing a percentage of the portfolio.\n\nBucket 1 (Year 1): 20% allocation  \n   - Buy $Y00-bond: a 1-year bond with $10 million face value (20% of $50 million target portfolio size)\n   - Consider a government bond or a high-grade corporate bond, e.g., a 1-year Treasury or a short-term commercial paper.\n\nBucket 2 (Year 2): 20% allocation  \n   - Buy $Y01-bond: a 2-year bond with $10 million face value (20% of $50 million target portfolio size)\n   - Choose a 2-year Treasury bond or a high-grade corporate bond with similar risk characteristics.\n\nBucket 3 (Year 3): 20% allocation  \n   - Buy $Y02-bond: a 3-year bond with $10 million face value (20% of $50 million target portfolio size)\n   - Consider a 3-year Treasury bond or a high-grade corporate bond with a credit rating similar to the bonds in the previous two buckets.\n\nBucket 4 (Year 4): 20% allocation  \n   - Buy $Y03-bond: a 4-year bond with $10 million face value (20% of $50 million target portfolio size)\n   - Choose a 4-year Treasury bond or a high-grade corporate bond with a credit rating at least BBB+.\n\nBucket 5 (Year 5): 20% allocation  \n   - Buy $Y04-bond: a 5-year bond with $10 million face value (20% of $50 million target portfolio size)\n   - Consider a 5-year Treasury bond or a high-grade corporate bond with similar risk characteristics.\n\nThe proposed allocation across the maturity buckets respects the constraint that no more than 30% of the portfolio can mature in any single year, while also maintaining an investment-grade rating for all securities.\n\nGiven the analysis and proposed ladder structure, the recommendation for this portfolio is to buy bonds with the proposed laddered maturity bucket structure within investment-grade limits.",
